Privacy Policy
--------------

Last Updated: May 28, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how this Service processes information when users send messages through the Application.
The Service is designed with privacy-by-design principles and minimizes the collection and retention of personal data.

i. Definitions
    For the purposes of this Agreement, the following terms shall have the meanings ascribed to them:
        - "Service" or "Application" refers to any part of the Roblox Chat Launcher client software, server Application, and associated endpoints.
        - "Guest User" or "Unverified User" refers to an individual who uses the Roblox Chat Launcher Service without linking a Roblox User ID.
        - "Verified User" refers to an individual who has voluntarily chosen to link their Roblox User ID with their Machine GUID.
        - "Creator" refers to an individual who has voluntarily chosen to register their Roblox Experience.
        - "Machine GUID" or "Hardware ID" refers to the unique registry key generated during a Windows installation.

ii. TL;DR
    We take steps to limit the data we can see, and aim to ensure only the minimum amount of data required for standard operations is collected.
    We CAN see the following information in our logs:
        - ✓ Your messages, which are never stored outside of logs and are automatically deleted after 7 days.
        - ✓ The channel your messages were sent on.
        - ✓ If you choose to verify your account, your Roblox User ID and Machine GUID in our database tables.
        - ✓ (Creators) If you generate an API key with us, your Roblox User ID, Universe ID, and Group ID (if applicable) in our database tables.
    We CANNOT see the following information in our logs:
        - ✗ Your public IP address or physical location.
        - ✗ Any permanent identifiers associated with messages, even if you are verified (if verified, your Roblox Username is only associated
             with your messages in the broadcasted message to other users in the same channel, which the server does not log).
        - ✗ Your Machine GUID, Roblox User ID, or Roblox Username associated with your messages, even if you are verified.
    Our hosting providers may have their own privacy policies, which you are encouraged to read.
    This section is not exhaustive. Please read below for the full Policy.

1. Data Transmission & IP Addresses
    To facilitate standard internet communication, your IP address is visible to our hosting provider (Render) to route messages back to your device.
        Data Minimization: Our server Application is designed so that it does not see, log, or store your public IP address, even in a hashed
                          or pseudonymized format.
        No Permanent Identifiers: We do not associate permanent identifiers, Roblox User IDs, or Roblox Usernames to messages in logs. The server handles
                                  routing by attaching a property to your in-memory WebSocket connection object (the temporary label derived from your
                                  current WebSocket connection port for Guest Users or Roblox Username for Verified Users).
        Client Visibility: Although the server does not associate identifiers to messages in logs, to facilitate standard chat functionality, the property
                           attached to your in-memory WebSocket connection object is broadcasted to other clients actively connected to the same channel.
                           This allows other users to see which speaker sent a specific message.
        Transient Identity: The server only sees the WebSocket connection port for both Guest Users and Verified Users in logs. This label is strictly
                            temporary; it changes every time you reconnect to the server. Users can manually trigger a reconnection and rotate their label
                            at any time by using the '/rc' command within the client.
        Open Source: Users may review the code to see exactly what data is processed and how it is handled at https://github.com/RobloxChatLauncher/RobloxChatLauncher.

2. Optional Roblox Account Verification
    Verification is a completely optional feature. We aim to ensure that users do not have to verify to access features that do not 
    fundamentally require identity confirmation.
        Hardware Identifiers: If you choose to verify your Roblox account via the profile blurb method, the Application reads the Machine 
                              GUID ("Hardware ID") on your local device. This ID is used to link your local installation to your Roblox 
                              User ID in our database.
        Storage & Persistence: If verified, your Hardware ID and associated Roblox User ID are stored in a persistent PostgreSQL database
                               (hosted on Neon) to recognize your account across sessions.
        No IP Logging: Even during verification, we do not log or store your IP address. The system relies solely on the Hardware ID provided 
                       by your device and the public data provided by the Roblox API.
        Right to Erasure: You may invoke your "Right to be Forgotten" at any time by running the '/unverify' command within the client. Executing
                          this command sends an immediate deletion request to our server, which permanently purges your Hardware ID and linked
                          Roblox User ID from our database and clears all associated data from your local device.
        Right to Erasure (Creators): Creators who wish to revoke their API key and delete their game registry data (Universe ID and linked Creator ID)
                                     may do so by contacting us at the email provided in the Contact & Privacy Inquiries section.

3. Creator API Access & Game Registry
    To facilitate the self-serve API system, we collect specific data required to authenticate your Roblox Experience.
        Data Collected: When you verify a game, we store your Roblox User ID (as the Creator), the Roblox Universe ID, the Roblox Group ID (if applicable) and a hashed API Key.
        Purpose: This data is strictly used to validate that incoming requests from Roblox servers are authorized to interact with the Roblox Chat Launcher API.
        Visibility Settings: By default, registered Universe IDs are marked as "Unlisted." If you choose to opt-in to public listings
                             (via the /settings endpoint), your Universe ID will be visible in our public API directory.
        Data Retention: This information is stored persistently in our PostgreSQL database (Neon) until you request deletion.

4. Message Content & Content Moderation
    Messages submitted to the Service are processed for the purpose of maintaining a safe and abuse-free environment. To assist with
    content moderation, message text is analyzed using the Perspective API. The Service enables Google's doNotStore option, which
    instructs Google not to retain submitted message text or use it for model training after analysis.
    Users are encouraged to review Google's Privacy Policy at https://policies.google.com/privacy.

5. Hosting & Infrastructure
    This Service is hosted on Render, and persistent data is stored on Neon. As hosting providers, Render and Neon may automatically collect
    technical metadata and retain access logs (such as IP addresses, timestamps, and database tables) for security and operational monitoring.
    In addition, message content may appear transiently within the Application logs as part of normal request handling.
        Retention: Render automatically deletes the Application logs after approximately 7 days. The Application itself does not persist or store
                   message content, chat history, or user-submitted messages outside of Render’s standard logging systems. The Service does not have the
                   ability to access, retrieve, or restore message content once Render’s logs are deleted.
    Users should avoid including personally identifiable or sensitive information in messages, as message content is user-submitted
    and cannot be guaranteed to remain private once transmitted.
    Users are encouraged to review Render's Privacy Policy at https://render.com/privacy and Neon's Privacy Policy at https://neon.com/privacy-policy.

6. Limited Personal Data Processing
    The Service is built on a "zero-account" model. We do not collect names, emails, or credentials.
        What the Server Sees: Your submitted message content, the specific channel/instance it is routed to, and (if verified) your Roblox User ID.
        Data Broadcast: To facilitate real-time chat functionality, the Server broadcasts your message content along with your associated user
                        identification (the temporary label for Guest Users, or the Roblox Username for Verified Users) to other connected clients
                        in the same channel. This data is transmitted dynamically and is not saved to any permanent database during the broadcast.
        Temporary Metadata: The server tracks active connections via ephemeral port numbers. Because these ports are reused by the operating system
                            across different users over time, they cannot be used as a reliable or permanent identifier for any specific individual.
        Verification: For Verified Users, we maintain a link between your Hardware ID and Roblox ID. Due to logs only being associated with transient
                      WebSocket ports, we generally cannot link a specific message to a specific person once the connection is closed.
    All processing is limited to what is necessary for Service operation, security, and abuse prevention.

7. Legal Basis & Consent
    GDPR / UK GDPR
        Where applicable, personal data is processed under Article 6(1)(f) (legitimate interests) for ensuring Service security, preventing abuse,
        and maintaining system integrity. Pursuant to Article 11 GDPR, we do not require, and do not collect, additional information to identify 
        users who choose not to use the optional verification feature.
            Rights Limitations: It is technically impossible to link a historical message to a specific individual once the connection is terminated.
                                Therefore, the rights of access, rectification, erasure, and portability (Articles 15–20) do not apply to historical message
                                data unless you provide additional identifying information that reasonably substantiates that a specific message was sent by you.
            Right to Complain: Regardless of identification, you maintain the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority.
    PIPEDA (Canada)
        Personal data is processed with implied consent for the limited purpose of Service security. In accordance with PIPEDA's principle of limited
        collection, we do not associate technical identifiers with specific individuals unless verification is voluntarily initiated. We reserve the 
        right to refuse access requests where the information cannot be reasonably associated with the requester without the collection of 
        additional personal data.
    CCPA / CPRA (California)
        The Service does not sell, rent, or share personal information as defined by the CCPA/CPRA. Personal information is processed solely to operate
        and secure the Service. We do not sell or share your personal information for cross-contextual behavioral advertising.
            Notice at Collection: We collect message content and (optionally) Hardware IDentifiers for security purposes. We do not sell or share this information.
            Verifiable Requests: California residents have the right to request deletion or access. However, we can only fulfill requests that are Verifiable.
                                 As we do not maintain traditional accounts, we may not be able to verify requests from Unverified Users. 

8. International Data Transfers
    This Service is hosted on servers located in the United States (via Render and Neon). When you use the Service, your data is transferred to and processed in the
    U.S. We ensure a similar degree of protection is afforded to it by ensuring that our sub-processors (Render, Neon, and Google) utilize standard contractual
    clauses (SCCs) or other legally recognized transfer mechanisms approved by the European Commission.

